{"full":"IppClub/YueScript","name":"YueScript","description":"A delightful language that compiles to Lua","category":"Other","language":"Lua","stars":614,"forks":45,"created":"2017-07-05T06:25:42Z","updated":"2026-09-30T09:53:17Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://yuescript.org","topics":["cpp","lua","moonscript","transpiler","yuescript"],"demo":"https://yuescript.org/try","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:46.208Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:46.208Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:46.208Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:45.074Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:17:51.392Z","stars":614,"forks":45},{"at":"2026-10-04T08:16:46.208Z","stars":614,"forks":45}],"technologies":[],"overviewAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T14:34:07.233Z","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Dynamic, expressive, and concise syntax for Lua development.","YueScript is a language that compiles to Lua. It is derived from MoonScript 0.5.0 and continues to adopt new features to stay up to date.","MoonScript has been used to build real-world projects such as Lapis, itch.io, and streak.club. MoonScript itself was also influenced by languages such as CoffeeScript. As the original implementation became harder to evolve without risking compatibility, YueScript was created as a modernized code base for pushing the language forward."],"features":["Based on a modified parserlib with performance enhancements. lpeg is no longer required.","Supports most MoonScript features and generates Lua code in a style compatible with the original compiler.","Preserves source line numbers in generated Lua to improve debugging.","Adds features like macros, existential operator, pipe operator, JavaScript-like export syntax, and more."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/IppClub/YueScript/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"efb2318d4b250f408be87b53e26085eb6c229aa8f0cf270210316258f91f8306","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T07:02:42.89